From e085cf45c6e0d2348abbad8a80a1f9d2491ed583 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 09:56:27 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Sections: count each face once where two segments meet (Fram
 Strait counted two faces twice)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

section_faces adds the faces of each segment of a section; where two segments meet their wedges can overlap by a cell
and the same face was counted by both (sign ±2). On the 15 km grid, Fram Strait's section did this at the 10°E
waypoint, in the West Spitsbergen Current (u(279, 215), v(278, 215)): over Sep-Dec 2005 Fram's southward transport came
out -0.26 Sv instead of -2.14 Sv on the box's boundary (GLORYS about -2.2), and the four gateways implied +2.1 m of sea
level inside them while it rose 1 cm (arctic_volume.jl, patches 092-093). The signs are now clamped to -1, 0, +1, with
a log line when a section had such faces. Davis, the BSO and Bering were not affected.

tsubouchi_comparison.jl takes `offline`: it then reads arctic_transports_offline.jld2 (analysis/transports.jl) and
writes tsubouchi_comparison_offline.md / .png, to recompute the gateway tables of runs made before this fix.
arctic_volume.jl draws the dashed line last, so it shows where it overlaps.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
